# chronologia leap-second table (UTC-TAI offset, cumulative)
#
# Source: IANA/IETF leap-seconds.list (mirrors the IERS Bulletin C / USNO
# TAI-UTC series), https://data.iana.org/time-zones/data/leap-seconds.list
# Downloaded: 2026-07-21
# Local copy cited at: ~/AgentWorkspaces/papers/standards/leap-seconds.list
# (see ~/AgentWorkspaces/papers/standards/INDEX.md)
#
# Format: two tab-separated columns per data row:
#   effective_utc_date<TAB>cumulative_tai_minus_utc_seconds
# `effective_utc_date` is the UTC calendar date on which the given offset
# takes effect (00:00:00 UTC that day); the leap second itself, when one is
# inserted, is dated the day before as 23:59:60 UTC.
#
# The first row (1972-01-01, 10) is the initial TAI-UTC offset fixed at the
# 1972 introduction of leap seconds, not a leap-second insertion. Every
# subsequent row is one inserted leap second (27 rows, 1972-06-30 through
# 2016-12-31 insertions), each raising the cumulative offset by exactly 1.
#
# table_valid_until: 2027-06-28 (the source list's `#@` expiry line — the
# date through which the list is confirmed complete absent a further IERS
# Bulletin C announcement; Bulletin C announces roughly six months ahead of
# any new leap second).
#
1972-01-01	10
1972-07-01	11
1973-01-01	12
1974-01-01	13
1975-01-01	14
1976-01-01	15
1977-01-01	16
1978-01-01	17
1979-01-01	18
1980-01-01	19
1981-07-01	20
1982-07-01	21
1983-07-01	22
